    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d295">

                <pb facs="0570" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg560"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 892.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 4, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your attention is invited to the
                    accompanying extract from a despatch of the 16th ultimo, No. 244, from Mr.
                    Dudley, the consul of the United States at Liverpool, respecting the small
                    steamer Alexandra, recently launched by the Messrs. Laird &amp; Brothers at
                    Birkenhead.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to give proper notice to her Majesty’s government in regard to
                    this vessel, and to support your representation by such corroborative evidence
                    of her character as you may be able to obtain.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. F. Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d295-a1.xml" xpointer="d295-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
